  "title": "Undertow",
  "tagline": "A borrowed camper van, a cold night by the sea, and a heater that should never have failed.",
  "setting": "Croyde · North Devon · November 2023",
  "sketchTitle": "CROYDE",
  "sketchCredit": "SKETCH: SITE VISIT, 22 NOVEMBER 2023 · NOT TO SCALE",
  "stayLabel": "Stay in Croyde",
  "briefing": [
    "Croyde, North Devon. Wednesday 22 November 2023. Out of season the village belongs to the surfers and the sheep: the car parks are empty, half the cottages are dark, and the wind comes straight off the Atlantic.",
    "On Friday morning Tess Rendle, 31, an A&E nurse at the hospital in Barnstaple, finished four night shifts in a row, and that evening she borrowed her brother’s camper van, Moss, to sleep by the sea. She parked at the clifftop car park at Marram Point. At 08:40 on Saturday the man who runs the café there found her dead inside, with the diesel heater still running. Carbon monoxide.",
    "The police vehicle examiner found the heater’s exhaust leaking into the van: no gasket in the joint, and the clamp loose. Her brother, Callum, builds camper vans for a living, and he fitted that heater himself. Nobody else is suspected. Callum has been interviewed under caution about his work, the coroner has the file, Trading Standards want his records, and online he is already ‘the van man who gassed his own sister’.",
    "Their mother, Ruth Rendle, has hired you. ‘Tess treated carbon monoxide poisoning every winter. She would never have slept next to a heater she didn’t trust. And Callum never skips a step — never. I’ve lost my daughter. Don’t let me lose my son as well.’",
    "Moss is in the police compound in Barnstaple, waiting for the coroner; Callum’s solicitor has arranged for you to see it. Callum has given you the keys to everything else."
  ],
